== 5.8 Chapter 5 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [A coup d'état is best defined as],
  [the constitutional removal of a president],
  [a mass uprising that changes the social order],
  [the sudden and illegal seizure of state power by a small group],
  [a refusal of soldiers to obey orders]
)

#mcq(2, [The first military coup in Nigeria took place on],
  [13 February 1976],
  [31 December 1983],
  [29 July 1966],
  [15 January 1966]
)

#mcq(3, [The first military head of state in Nigeria was],
  [Olusegun Obasanjo],
  [Yakubu Gowon],
  [Murtala Muhammed],
  [Johnson Aguiyi-Ironsi]
)

#mcq(4, [The July 1966 counter-coup brought to power],
  [Murtala Muhammed],
  [Yakubu Gowon],
  [Johnson Aguiyi-Ironsi],
  [Sani Abacha]
)

#mcq(5, [The Nigerian Civil War lasted from],
  [1966 to 1969],
  [1967 to 1970],
  [1967 to 1971],
  [1970 to 1973]
)

#mcq(6, [The military government that created twelve states in Nigeria was led by],
  [Gowon],
  [Ironsi],
  [Murtala],
  [Babangida]
)

#mcq(7, [Murtala Muhammed was assassinated on],
  [29 July 1975],
  [15 January 1966],
  [1 October 1979],
  [13 February 1976]
)

#mcq(8, [The head of state who handed over to a civilian government in 1979 was],
