  #block(breakable: false)[
  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A coup is sudden, illegal and carried out by a small group, usually soldiers. A revolution is mass-based, a mutiny is a refusal of orders, and impeachment is constitutional.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    15 January 1966, led by Major Kaduna Nzeogwu and other officers. July 1966 is the counter-coup, February 1976 the Dimka attempt and December 1983 the Buhari coup.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Major-General J. T. U. Aguiyi-Ironsi took over after the January 1966 coup and was killed in the July counter-coup.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Gowon became head of state after the counter-coup of 29 July 1966, which also killed Ironsi.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    July 1967 to January 1970, when the Biafran forces surrendered. The war dominated Gowon's government.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Gowon created twelve states in 1967, abolishing the regions. Murtala created nineteen in 1976, and Abacha thirty-six in 1996.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    13 February 1976, in the failed Dimka coup. 29 July 1975 is the coup that brought him to power, and 1979 the handover.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Obasanjo, who took over after Murtala's assassination and handed over to Shagari on 1 October 1979.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    1 October 1979, with Shagari's inauguration. 1983 is the coup that ended it, 1993 the annulled election and 1999 the Fourth Republic.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    31 December 1983, by the coup led by Muhammadu Buhari. Babangida's coup followed in August 1985.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    December 1983 to August 1985, when Babangida overthrew him. It is remembered for the War Against Indiscipline and Decree No. 4.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    27 August 1985. He ruled until August 1993, when he stepped aside after annulling the June 12 election.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Babangida annulled the election, widely believed to have been won by Moshood Abiola, and later stepped aside.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Shonekan was appointed by Babangida in August 1993 and resigned in November 1993, when Abacha took power.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    17 November 1993. He ruled until his death on 8 June 1998.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Obasanjo was elected and sworn in on 29 May 1999, after Abubakar's transition programme.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The clause ousts the court's jurisdiction, so the decree cannot be challenged. It is the single most examined instrument of military rule.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    An edict is made by a state military administrator; a decree is made by the federal military government.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The tribunals tried civilians for offences such as treason and currency trafficking, often without appeal to the ordinary courts.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Intervention is explained by the weakness of civilian institutions, corruption and rigged elections. A strong parliament and judiciary are defences against it.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Abolishing the regions removed the only units with the standing to challenge the centre, and the new states were smaller and more dependent.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The decision to move the capital to Abuja was taken in 1976 under Murtala, and the territory was carved out then.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The reform gave local government a uniform structure and recognised it as a third tier, which is the date the paper attaches to local government reform.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    1975, at Lagos. The OAU was founded in 1963, and ECOMOG intervened in Liberia in 1990.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    State creation, the FCT, the local government reform and ECOWAS are the standard credits. Free elections and civilian institutions were the casualties, not the achievements.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Ouster clauses, detention without trial and the Abacha record are the standard debits. The other three are the credits.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    July 1966 is the classic case: it removed the government that January 1966 had installed. A failed coup is an attempted coup, not a counter-coup.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The attempt killed the head of state, but the plotters were defeated and Obasanjo took over. It is the classic Nigerian example of an attempted coup.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The suspension was a justification and a technique: the legal order was set aside, and the decree replaced it.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Parties and parliaments lost the chance to learn their trade, and the ouster clause bred impunity. Military rule did not strengthen parliament or end corruption.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Abubakar took over on Abacha's death in 1998 and ran a short transition that produced the 1999 Constitution and the Fourth Republic.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Gowon ruled through the civil war and created twelve states in 1967. The annulment and the FCT belong to later governments.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Buhari's government (1983–85) launched WAI, a campaign for orderliness and civic discipline. Babangida's programme was the Structural Adjustment Programme.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The absence of a peaceful means of removal is the defining weakness of any military government. It is not criticised for holding too many elections.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The special tribunals were set up outside the ordinary court system, which is why they are treated as an instrument of military rule.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The first coup suspended the Republican Constitution, beginning the military period. The 1979 Constitution ended it, and the 1999 Constitution belongs to the Fourth Republic.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    State creation, the abolition of the regions and the concentration of revenue all strengthened the centre, which is the federalism point the paper draws from Chapter 5.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Abubakar ran the transition that produced the 1999 Constitution and the election of Obasanjo.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Abacha created six states in 1996, bringing the total to thirty-six. Babangida created nine in 1991 and Abubakar handed over in 1999.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Abubakar's government promulgated the Constitution in 1999 and handed over to Obasanjo on 29 May 1999. Obasanjo governed under it, he did not promulgate it.
  ]

]

